Today we’re releasing the Bonsai Image 4B family. Inspired by the art of bonsai, it makes models smaller without losing quality. The Bonsai treatment was applied to FLUX.2 Klein 4B, keeping the structure, making it compact, and preserving beauty.

The result includes a 1-bit Bonsai Image 4B at 0.93 GB and a ternary version at 1.21 GB. These models enable high-quality diffusion inference on local hardware, from laptops to phones, bringing more ways to create closer to you and under your control.

@PrismML: "Today we’re releasing 1-bit and Ternary Bonsai Image 4B, a new family of image-generation models designed to run high-quality diffusion inference on local hardware: from laptops to phones."

First tests on my 12GB RTX 3060 with the new PrismML Ternary Bonsai Image 4B model are actually impressive. It generates 1408×704 images in about 2.8 seconds (4 steps), uses peak VRAM under 7GB, and is extremely consistent. This might be the best text-to-image model you can run on small consumer cards right now.

Better benchmark results are being prepared, and will be shared soon.

